--========check and install pgaudit  ( sysops bayad repository ro mount kone)

apt search pgaudit
apt-get install postgresql-XX-pgaudit  # replace XX with your PostgreSQL version



======Add extention to config file


1. Edit postgresql.conf: Locate the postgresql.conf file, usually found in the PostgreSQL data directory. 

cat /var/lib/pgsql/12/data/postgresql.conf | grep shared_preload_libraries

---As the root user, add or modify the following configuration settings: 

shared_preload_libraries = 'pgaudit'



2. Restart PostgreSQL: Restart the PostgreSQL service to apply the changes

systemctl restart PostgreSQL 

3. Create the extension in the database

a:  Connect to your PostgreSQL instance:

psql

b: Create the extension in the desired database:

CREATE EXTENSION pgaudit;

4. Verify installation

SELECT * FROM pg_extension WHERE extname = 'pgaudit';

